    "text": "### What this page is for\nEvery product the store can sell, in one sheet you can flick through and correct. Products arrive here from supplier price lists (Store → Data Feeds → a supplier → Import into store, or an automatic feed) and from Add product for a one-off that no feed carries.\n### Going live\nImported products start offline: they are in the catalogue but not on the website. Tick the ones you want and press Go live; they appear in the store within five minutes, under their category and in New Arrivals. Take offline removes ticked products from the website without losing them. The Website column and filter show which are live. Start with a few, check their photos and prices on the website, then put the rest live. A product with no photo or description is not put live straight away: it is looked up on its manufacturer's website first (see Photos & text) and goes live when it has both.\n### Finding and ticking products\nThe sheet shows 100 products at a time. Search, the filters and the page buttons under the sheet find what you want, and every page is sorted by name. The box at the top of the first column ticks every product on the page; then Tick all and the number matching ticks every product the filters match, on every page. Ticks and unsaved edits stay while you change page or filters.\n### Columns\n- Cost is what the supplier charges us, ex GST. RRP is the shelf price, inc GST; Ex GST is RRP ÷ 1.1.\n- Margin is Ex GST minus Cost, in dollars and as a percentage of Ex GST. Red is below cost, amber under 15%.\n- Member / Silver / Gold / Platinum are what each customer tier pays: cost plus that tier's markup from the Pricing page, plus GST, never above RRP.\n- Category is the store category the product is listed under. For feed products it comes from the supplier's category, mapped on the supplier's Data Feeds page.\n- Active off takes a product out of the store without losing it: the row stays so a re-import updates it rather than duplicating it, and its history survives. An inactive row shows Delete permanently if you really want it gone -- but if a supplier feed still lists the SKU, the next pull creates it again.\n### Editing\nType straight into a row -- name, brand, category, supplier, cost, RRP, stock, active -- and its Save button appears; each save is recorded in the audit log with the before and after values.\n### Re-price from cost\nSets RRP = Cost × (1 + markup) × 1.1 (GST), rounded to the nearest 5 cents, for every product the filters match (on all pages) or for one supplier. Preview shows how many would change and a few examples; nothing moves until you click Apply. Products without a cost are skipped.\n### Export\nExport CSV downloads every product the filters match, on all pages, with every column."
